<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">North West Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1779">1779</a>–<a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The North West Company was a fur-trading partnership based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> that competed fiercely with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> across western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. Its traders and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> allies pushed far inland and opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a>, a conflict that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-seven-oaks">Battle of Seven Oaks</a> in 1816. It merged with the Hudson's Bay Company in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-west-company.jpg" alt="North West Company" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_West_Company_-_Coat_Of_Arms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
